00:37:33.000 --> 00:37:55.000
eye. Can you tell me about the work that you and your colleagues have done to test the idea of adopting what's called a fly-on-the-wall perspective on our own problems? Yeah. So when we think about negative experiences or when we anticipate future ones as well, we often have mental imagery surrounding it. And research has shown that we can think

81
00:37:55.000 --> 00:38:18.000
about different experiences in our lives from different perspectives. So you can conjure up a mental snapshot of a past event and actually replay it happening in your own mind from a first person perspective. Or you can also think about that same experience, but from a third person perspective, like a fly on the wall peering down on the scene.

82
00:38:18.000 --> 00:38:42.000
